# Project Topology

- `vektre` (this repo): the NestJS backend API + the Hocuspocus/Yjs
  collaboration server (`src/collaboration-yjs/yjs-server.ts`).
- `vektre-web` (sibling repo, `../vektre-web`): the marketing/venture
  **website**. It is NOT the product frontend/client app.
- The actual product frontend (the desktop app end users run) lives on the
  user's desktop machine, outside this VPS entirely. It is not present in
  this workspace, in `vektre-web`, or anywhere on this VPS — there is no
  frontend source code accessible here to read or edit.

## Implications

- Never refer to `vektre-web` as "the frontend" or assume UI/collaboration
  client wiring questions can be answered by reading `vektre-web` source.
- When diagnosing client-side issues (e.g. collaboration/WebSocket bugs,
  Yjs provider usage), the relevant client code is on the user's desktop
  and not inspectable here — reason from the backend's API contracts
  (REST responses, `collabWsUrl`, env vars) and ask the user for
  desktop-app-side logs/behavior instead of searching this VPS for it.
- Backend changes that affect the frontend (new endpoints, response shape
  changes, env var requirements) should be called out explicitly since
  there's no way to verify frontend integration from this workspace.
